  "worked_solution": "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n\ufeff\ufeff\ufeff\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\left|\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}\\right| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-3(-3) & =0 \\\\ 4-4\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+9 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +13 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(-4)\\pm \\sqrt{(-4)^{2}-4(1)(13)}}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm \\sqrt{-36}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm 6\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =2\\pm 3\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =2\\pm 3\\text{i}.$",
